WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Wendy, they're dead!

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Brody, pull it together.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
We don't have a chance, okay?

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
We have to get out of here now!

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
No, Brody.We are not leaving.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
We have got to find my sister.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
No!

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
No, I am getting out of here right now!

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Brody!

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Brody, get back here!

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Brody!

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
God, you son of a bitch!

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:15.730
Cut.

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.650
What the hell was that?

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:20.580
Thanks.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:23.570
Here you go.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:24.840
Thanks, Walter.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:26.340
Don't mark that.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:30.400
It's all good, Tara.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.860
That was great.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.050
Uh, let's do it again.

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:36.740
Uh, maybe we try dialing
up that scream, huh?

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:37.650
I know, I know.

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.920
I'm just -- I'm having
trouble with the tennis ball.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.170
That is just for cg registration.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:45.980
When ivan and the fx guys are done,
it is going to look terrifying.

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:48.740
You want to look at the
concept sketches again?

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:49.770
No, that's okay.

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:50.640
I'll find it.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.210
I know you will, pumpkin, huh?

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:53.100
Okay.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.460
Going again, everybody.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:58.090
10-Minute reload for camera and sound.

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:00.240
No, man, I'm telling you.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:05.640
Working alone behind the sets or after
wrap, I catch this weird vibe sometimes.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.130
Like what?

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:09.100
Mmm, like something's watching.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.090
Come on.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:12.340
Hey.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.040
Working on a movie like this?

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.180
Weird crap's bound to happen.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:19.790
Frank thinks the stage is
haunted. Like, for real.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:25.950
All I'm saying is, they call wrap,
I get done, and I get out of here.

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:28.470
Fast.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:36.480
Guy is definitely off his meds.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:43.670
Brody, come back.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.130
You son of a bitch.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.770
Brody, come back, you son of a bitch.

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:01.010
Hello?

00:02:06.689 --> 00:02:08.300
Guys?

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:14.689
Come on.

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.689
It's not funny.

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:18.780
Okay.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.920
Ha ha, very funny.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:27.680
Hello?

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.390
Who's there?

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:53.850
Now, that's what I'm talking about!

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:15.370
First opened in 1927, the lot has been
in continuous operation for eight decades.

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:17.920
Hey, you know this is where
they filmed "Creepshow"?

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:22.650
Now to the right here is Stars Hollow.

00:03:23.819 --> 00:03:27.500
It's the setting for the
television series "Gilmore Girls."

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:33.129
And if we're lucky, we might even
catch one of the show's stars.

00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:34.580
Come on.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:36.259
Let's finish the tour.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:43.150
And then up to the right here, we have New York
Avenue, and that's where they shot "Lois & Clark."

00:03:47.699 --> 00:03:48.590
Sammy, check it out.

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:50.199
It's matt damon.

00:03:51.069 --> 00:03:51.540
Yeah.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:52.840
I'm pretty sure that's not Matt Damon.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:53.699
No, it is.

00:03:53.699 --> 00:03:56.660
Well, Matt Damon just picked
up a broom and started sweeping.

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:58.810
Yeah, he was probably
researching a role or something.

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:00.950
Uh, I don't think so.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:02.220
Hey, this way.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:04.290
Uh, I think stage 9's over here.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:04.889
Come on, man.

00:04:04.889 --> 00:04:05.879
Let's keep going this way.

00:04:05.879 --> 00:04:06.610
No, come on.

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:07.370
We got to work.

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:08.060
Golly.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:09.250
Dude, you wanted to come to L.A.

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:10.450
Yeah, for a vacation!

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.819
I mean, swimming pools and movie stars!

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:13.879
Not to work.

00:04:13.879 --> 00:04:16.400
This seem like swimming
pool weather to you, Dean?

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.870
It's practically canadian.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:19.139
Yeah.

00:04:19.139 --> 00:04:24.830
I just figured that, you know, after everything that happened
with madison, you could use a little R&R,  that's all.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:25.900
Maybe I want to work, Dean.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:27.199
Maybe it keeps my mind off things.

00:04:27.199 --> 00:04:29.110
Okay, okay, all right.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:31.939
So this crew guy, what,
did he ...he died on set?

00:04:31.939 --> 00:04:35.270
Yeah, rumors spreading
like wildfire online.

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:37.379
They're saying the set's haunted.

00:04:37.379 --> 00:04:38.930
Like "poltergeist"?

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:40.270
Could be a poltergeist.

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:40.840
No, no, no.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.530
The movie "poltergeist."

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:45.020
You know nothing of your
cultural heritage, do you?

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:52.120
It was rumored that the set of "poltergeist" was
cursed, that they used real human bones as props.

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:54.710
Like, at least three of
the actors died in it.

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:57.920
Yeah, might be something like that.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:58.850
All right, so this crew guy.

00:04:58.850 --> 00:04:59.790
What's his name?

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:01.040
Frank Jaffe.

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:03.189
You got a death certificate
or a coroner's report?

00:05:03.189 --> 00:05:06.030
Well, no, but, uh, it's L.A., You know?

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:07.450
That might not even be his real name.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:11.230
But the girl who found him, she said
she saw something ... a vanishing figure.

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:12.230
What's the girl's name?

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:13.189
Uh, Tara Benchley.

00:05:13.189 --> 00:05:15.370
Whoa, Tara Benchley?

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:18.370
From "feardotcom" and
"ghost ship" Tara Benchley?

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:20.210
Dude, why didn't you say so?

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:23.550
So now you're suddenly on board?

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:26.220
I mean, I'm a fan of her work.

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:28.600
It's very good.

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:31.900
No, look.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:32.620
Don't get me wrong.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:35.530
Everyone at this studio loves
the dailies, myself included.

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:38.100
We were just wondering if it could be...

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.960
You know, a little brighter.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:41.580
Brighter?

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:43.759
Yeah, Jay, more color.

00:05:43.759 --> 00:05:44.900
Mcg, you know what I'm saying.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.250
You're the master of that stuff.

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:47.990
Brad, this is a horror movie.

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:49.660
Who says horror has to be dark?

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:52.830
It's just -- It's sort of
depressing, don't you think?

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:53.759
Uh, excuse me.

00:05:53.759 --> 00:05:55.639
Uh, green-Shirt guy?

00:05:55.639 --> 00:05:57.220
Yeah, yeah, you.Come here.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:02.250
Can you get me a, uh,
smoothie from craft?

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:05.170
You want a what from who?

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:08.360
You are a P.A.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:09.670
This is what you do.

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:11.650
Yeah, he, uh...

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:14.139
One smoothie coming right up.

00:06:17.689 --> 00:06:18.639
What's a P.A.?

00:06:18.639 --> 00:06:20.689
I think they're kind of like slaves.

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:26.210
They'll let anybody
in this business, huh?

00:07:01.149 --> 00:07:03.300
6, 6, 6. Mark.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:06.730
Ready!

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:09.610
Okay, why don't we take it
from, "come on, it'll be fun"?

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:10.830
And action.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:11.389
Come on.

00:07:11.389 --> 00:07:12.769
It'll be fun.

00:07:44.529 --> 00:07:47.700
Dicta sunt explicabo.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:49.110
God, I hate you so much right now.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:50.289
Cut!

00:07:51.139 --> 00:07:52.470
Very nice.

00:07:53.919 --> 00:07:55.039
So?

00:07:55.039 --> 00:07:56.820
No emf anywhere.

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:57.509
Great.

00:07:57.509 --> 00:07:58.300
So, what do you think?

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:01.310
Well, I think being a P.A.Sucks, but...

00:08:02.389 --> 00:08:03.330
But the food these people get?

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:03.950
Are you kidding me?

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.370
I mean, look at these things.

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:08.600
They're like miniature
philly cheesesteak sandwiches.

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:10.050
They're delicious.

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:12.529
Maybe later.

00:08:15.279 --> 00:08:17.169
What did you find out
about the dead crew guy?

00:08:20.509 --> 00:08:23.139
Uh, Frank Jaffe was just
filling in for the day.

00:08:23.139 --> 00:08:25.480
Nobody here knew him or
where he lived or anything.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:26.060
Oh, great.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:27.310
So you found out about as much as I did.

00:08:28.669 --> 00:08:29.230
Hey, guys.

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:30.279
Oh, hey.

00:08:30.279 --> 00:08:31.740
They're wonderful.

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:32.789
Listen.

00:08:32.789 --> 00:08:34.960
I did dig up some stuff
about stage 9's history.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:40.370
Four people died messy here over the past 80
years, two suicides and two fatal accidents.

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:42.000
Any one of those could
be a vengeful spirit.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.330
Yeah.

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:45.210
Just got to narrow it down more.

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:52.259
I'll get right on that.

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:05.370
Hey, are you supposed
to get one of these?

00:09:11.269 --> 00:09:13.029
I..I don't really know what I'm doing.

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:15.169
First day?

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:17.090
Yeah, my big break.

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:23.659
You know, I know it's really uncool
to say this, but I'm a big fan.

00:09:23.710 --> 00:09:24.860
I loved you in "boogeyman."

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:25.840
Oh, god.

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:27.870
What a terrible script.

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:29.210
Uh, but, thank you.

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:30.720
Yeah.

00:09:33.279 --> 00:09:34.700
You found him, right?

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:36.960
The -- The
dead guy?

00:09:40.789 --> 00:09:41.440
I'm sorry.

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:42.830
You probably don't
want to talk about this.

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:45.300
No, no, actually,
it's -- It's okay.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:48.769
Nobody around here really
brings it up very much.

00:09:48.769 --> 00:09:51.230
I think they're all scared I'm
gonna have some kind of breakdown.

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:54.129
That must have been awful.

00:09:57.190 --> 00:09:58.419
What happened?

00:09:58.659 --> 00:10:00.210
It was horrible.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:07.840
There ... there was all this blood coming
from his eyes, from his mouth, and, uh...

00:10:09.399 --> 00:10:11.100
I saw this, um...

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:14.940
What?

00:10:18.379 --> 00:10:20.120
I saw this shape.

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:24.080
To tell you the truth, I
don't know actually what I saw.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:25.879
I just know I saw it.

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:27.940
Thanks, Walter.

00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:35.050
Uh, so this -- This crew
guy Frank, did you know him?

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:37.250
No, not that well.

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:37.840
That's funny.

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:40.310
It's like no one around
here actually knew the guy.

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:41.590
I got his picture.

00:10:42.539 --> 00:10:43.470
You do?

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:44.259
Yeah.

00:10:44.259 --> 00:10:46.620
I take polaroids of all the crew.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:49.310
It's just one of those things
you do to kill time on the set.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:54.600
Right there.

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:01.940
Son of a bitch.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:10.320
Gerard st.James?

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:11.590
Yes?

00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:14.419
You're still alive, and
you're not Frank Jaffe.

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:15.620
NO

00:11:15.620 --> 00:11:20.289
You were -- You were desert soldier number 4
in "Metalstorm: The destruction of jared-Syn."

00:11:20.289 --> 00:11:21.169
I was.

00:11:21.169 --> 00:11:22.879
I knew I recognized you.

00:11:22.879 --> 00:11:24.779
I am a huge fan.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:29.730
I mean, your turn as the tractor-Crash
victim in "Critters 3" ...wow.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:31.680
Hey, well, please.

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:32.450
Come in.

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:42.379
Thanks.

00:11:42.379 --> 00:11:43.580
Yeah, it was the producers.

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:45.720
I mean, they brought me in
for the day to play Frank.

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:47.870
Just to fake your death?

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:50.379
Well, rumors of a haunted film set...

00:11:50.379 --> 00:11:56.990
Free publicity, especially when you're making a horror
movie I mean, it's already all over the internet.

00:11:56.990 --> 00:11:58.610
Yeah, we know.

00:11:59.389 --> 00:12:03.159
These days, it's all about
new media, building buzz.

00:12:03.159 --> 00:12:06.360
They say I'm the new "lonelygirl."

00:12:07.139 --> 00:12:07.950
Who?

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:09.870
And the ghost Tara saw?

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:12.389
Projected on a screen of diffusion.

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:15.100
Isn't that kind of cruel...

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:16.490
Messing with their heads like that?

00:12:16.490 --> 00:12:18.500
Hey, I just play the part.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:20.149
I don't write the script.

00:12:20.149 --> 00:12:22.120
Speaking of...

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:28.580
I'm playing willy in a dinner-Theater production
of "salesman" at costa mesa all next month.

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:31.539
Get a free pepper steak with the coupon.

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:33.289
Well, now, wait a second.

00:12:33.289 --> 00:12:35.620
If you're seen in public,
won't that ruin the hoax?

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:36.860
Oh, please.

00:12:37.389 --> 00:12:40.519
Frank and willy, , ,
totally different characters.

00:12:40.519 --> 00:12:41.870
You know what?

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:43.870
Thanks very much, Mr. Saint.James.

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:44.860
It was just nagging at us.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:49.930
But we're ...we're very glad,
you know, you're alive and well.

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:51.269
Yeah.

00:12:53.289 --> 00:12:54.399
Absolutely.

00:12:54.399 --> 00:12:56.430
I wanted to ask you.

00:12:56.430 --> 00:12:58.919
What was it like working
with Richard Moll?

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:03.960
He's from "metalstorm."

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:07.220
He was Hurok, King
of the Cyclops people.

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:10.120
Gentleman's gentleman.

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:11.490
Yeah?

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:13.730
All right.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:15.210
Pepper steak.

00:13:17.970 --> 00:13:22.450
When we read from that book, we must
have brought them back...back from hell.

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:25.600
Now they're trying to use us...

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:26.990
It doesn't matter.

00:13:27.070 --> 00:13:29.139
We're not going till we
find Wendy and her sister.

00:13:29.139 --> 00:13:30.490
Got it?

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:31.409
Good.

00:13:31.409 --> 00:13:33.019
Now, let's get busy.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:35.800
Cut!

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:36.659
No good for sound.

00:13:36.659 --> 00:13:38.600
I'm getting some kind of feedback.

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:43.269
Another costly sound delay.

00:13:43.269 --> 00:13:45.169
All right, we're going
again for sound, people!

00:13:45.169 --> 00:13:46.629
Thank you!

00:13:46.879 --> 00:13:50.039
No, it's a great scene,
really ..Dynamite.

00:13:50.039 --> 00:13:51.190
But I still got a few...

00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:54.440
Not -- Not problems,
just questions.

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:55.779
Like what?

00:13:56.200 --> 00:14:00.389
Well, for one thing. The rules
aren't really landing for me.

00:14:00.389 --> 00:14:05.680
Like, the kids do this latin chant,
and that makes the ghosts show up?

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:06.769
Yeah.

00:14:06.769 --> 00:14:09.779
If the ghosts are in hell,
how do they hear the chanting?

00:14:09.779 --> 00:14:12.690
I mean, what, do they
have super hearing?

00:14:12.690 --> 00:14:13.789
Well, it's a logic bump.

00:14:13.789 --> 00:14:15.419
The rules don't track.

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:18.190
Marty, you're the writer.

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:19.800
What about throwing in an explainer?

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:20.560
Yeah, that'd be super.

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:22.180
I got to check some messages.

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:26.800
Suits.

00:14:43.669 --> 00:14:45.370
Has mcg seen this?

00:14:45.539 --> 00:14:50.450
I like the whole body-Paint,
black-And-White thing, but, gee, I...

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:54.570
I don't think those neck wounds
are really gonna read on-Camera.

00:14:54.769 --> 00:14:56.879
They need to be red.

00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:58.580
You know what I'm saying?

00:14:58.740 --> 00:14:59.759
Hey, Jay!

00:14:59.759 --> 00:15:01.750
I need to speak to makeup.

00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:05.450
Yeah?

00:15:25.159 --> 00:15:26.570
Wait up.

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:31.159
When we read from that book, we must
have brought them back ...back from hell.

00:15:31.159 --> 00:15:32.370
I don't understand.

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:34.560
If they were in hell, how
could they hear our chanting?

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:36.490
They must have super hearing.

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:11.250
Wendy?

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:12.090
Oh, Mitch!

00:16:12.090 --> 00:16:13.340
God, you're alive!

00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:15.110
You won't get rid of me that easy.

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:17.360
Rumble, rumble, rumble!

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:19.379
Salt.

00:16:19.379 --> 00:16:20.360
Okay, we need salt.

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:23.550
I read in that book that
it keeps ghosts away.

00:16:23.550 --> 00:16:26.500
Kendra, logan, you guys check the back.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:29.790
The poor bastard killed
himself, like, for real.

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:31.500
Shouldn't we shut it down or something?

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:34.139
We had a moment of silence
for him at breakfast.

00:16:34.139 --> 00:16:35.929
He was just a studio guy.

00:16:35.929 --> 00:16:37.340
Shh.

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:38.459
I love you.

00:16:38.459 --> 00:16:39.370
I know.

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:42.280
I'm sorry.

00:16:44.219 --> 00:16:46.949
Can we ...can we cut or something?

00:16:46.949 --> 00:16:49.310
Uh, yeah.

00:16:49.310 --> 00:16:49.709
Cut.

00:16:49.709 --> 00:16:50.490
Cut!

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:51.679
That's a cut!

00:16:54.899 --> 00:16:56.510
Only I get to say "cut."

00:16:57.929 --> 00:16:59.449
Hey, what's up?

00:16:59.449 --> 00:17:01.310
I'm just a little upset.

00:17:01.719 --> 00:17:04.960
With everything that's been
going on, who can blame you?

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:07.860
I just can't wrap my head
around the dialogue, you know?

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:10.079
"Salt" -- Doesn't
that sound silly?

00:17:10.079 --> 00:17:12.590
I mean, why would a
ghost be afraid of salt?

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:14.210
Okay, um...

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:16.820
Marty, what do you think?

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:18.329
Not married to salt.

00:17:18.329 --> 00:17:18.880
What do you want?

00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:20.690
We still sticking with condiments?

00:17:20.690 --> 00:17:23.650
Mmm, it just sounds
different, not better.

00:17:23.650 --> 00:17:25.230
What else would a ghost be scared of?

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:26.990
Oh, you got to be kidding me.

00:17:26.990 --> 00:17:29.510
What would a ghost be scared of?

00:17:29.510 --> 00:17:31.269
Maybe shotguns.

00:17:31.269 --> 00:17:34.730
That makes even less sense than salt.

00:17:36.090 --> 00:17:37.480
These people are idiots.

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:43.389
Walter's a little testy for a P.A., Huh?

00:17:43.389 --> 00:17:44.619
How's it going in here?

00:17:44.619 --> 00:17:50.039
Really good -- Tara has stepped up her performance,
and I think it's from the sense-Memory stuff.

00:17:50.039 --> 00:17:50.880
Sense-Memory?

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:52.000
Yeah.

00:17:53.909 --> 00:17:56.840
Dean, you know, when I ask how it's going
here, I'm talking about the case, right?

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:58.440
We don't really work here.

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:00.349
You know, I thought
you hated being a P.A.

00:18:03.469 --> 00:18:04.099
I don't know.

00:18:04.099 --> 00:18:04.840
It's not so bad.

00:18:04.840 --> 00:18:06.699
I kind of feel like part
of the team, you know?

00:18:06.699 --> 00:18:07.530
It's good.

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:08.639
Oh, taquito?

00:18:08.639 --> 00:18:09.809
They're wonderful.

00:18:09.809 --> 00:18:10.639
No.

00:18:10.639 --> 00:18:12.570
Um, listen.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:14.139
I conned my way into the morgue.

00:18:14.139 --> 00:18:16.099
News reports are right.

00:18:16.099 --> 00:18:17.750
Brad's a doornail
-- No question.

00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:18.780
Copy that.

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:19.519
Sorry.What?

00:18:19.519 --> 00:18:20.380
"Copy that"?

00:18:20.380 --> 00:18:21.150
What did you say?

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:22.280
The news reports are right.

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:23.119
Brad's a doornail.

00:18:23.119 --> 00:18:24.030
They're aware.

00:18:24.030 --> 00:18:24.949
Who's aware?

00:18:24.949 --> 00:18:25.630
Sorry.

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:26.570
What were you saying?

00:18:26.570 --> 00:18:29.550
Uh, uh, the newspaper's right.

00:18:29.550 --> 00:18:30.500
Brad's a doornail.

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:31.440
No question about it.

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:33.199
I guess it's a good
thing we didn't skip town.

00:18:33.199 --> 00:18:34.179
Oh, come here.

00:18:34.179 --> 00:18:35.619
I want you to hear something.

00:18:35.619 --> 00:18:36.539
Copy that.

00:18:36.539 --> 00:18:37.820
On my way.

00:18:39.949 --> 00:18:40.590
Hey, Dave.

00:18:40.820 --> 00:18:42.650
Can you play that thing
you were playing me earlier?

00:18:42.650 --> 00:18:44.019
Sure.

00:18:44.019 --> 00:18:45.829
Thanks.

00:18:49.360 --> 00:18:50.650
It doesn't matter.

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:52.949
We're not leaving till we
find Wendy and her sister.

00:18:52.949 --> 00:18:54.199
Got it?

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:55.349
Good.

00:18:55.349 --> 00:18:57.039
Now, let's get busy.

00:19:00.269 --> 00:19:01.280
E.V.P.

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:02.990
From the night of Brad's stage dive.

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:06.139
All of a sudden, I'm getting
electromagnetic readings up the wazoo.

00:19:06.139 --> 00:19:08.320
For some reason, it's
a legit haunting now.

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:09.090
Well, whose ghost, Dean?

00:19:09.090 --> 00:19:09.820
What's it want?

00:19:09.820 --> 00:19:12.409
I think we should take a
look at Brad's death scene.

00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:35.659
Now, where'd you get this dvd?

00:19:35.659 --> 00:19:37.199
They're called dailies.

00:19:37.199 --> 00:19:38.380
I got it from cindy.

00:19:38.380 --> 00:19:40.590
She's kind of got this
thing going with drew.

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:42.329
He dubbed me an extra copy.

00:19:45.619 --> 00:19:46.059
All right.

00:19:46.059 --> 00:19:47.760
Here's where the guy
fell through the roof.

00:19:47.760 --> 00:19:49.280
Right.

00:19:51.139 --> 00:19:52.250
All right, here we go.

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:54.050
They must have super hearing.

00:19:57.909 --> 00:19:58.510
Wait.

00:19:58.510 --> 00:19:59.820
Go back, go back.

00:20:00.929 --> 00:20:02.980
Right after -- Right
after -- Yeah, right.

00:20:04.079 --> 00:20:05.050
Wait.

00:20:07.050 --> 00:20:08.409
There.

00:20:11.099 --> 00:20:13.269
It's like "3 men and
a baby" all over again.

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:19.369
Selleck, danson, and guttenberg,
and I don't know who played the baby.

00:20:19.369 --> 00:20:20.500
What's your point?

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:24.090
There's a scene where people say that
the camera caught a ghost on film.

00:20:24.090 --> 00:20:27.320
Apparently, in the background of one of the
scenes, there was this boy that nobody remembers.

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:29.240
Spirit photography.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:34.940
I've seen her before.

00:20:40.909 --> 00:20:42.070
Here.Check this out.

00:20:43.980 --> 00:20:45.480
Yeah, go for ozzie.

00:20:47.719 --> 00:20:49.280
No, I don't have a 20 on Tara.

00:20:49.280 --> 00:20:50.269
I think she's 10-100.

00:20:52.409 --> 00:20:53.909
Okay, copy that.

00:20:54.860 --> 00:20:55.240
I'm sorry.

00:20:55.240 --> 00:20:56.630
What were you saying?

00:20:59.079 --> 00:21:02.480
Elise Drummond. Starlet
back in the '30s.

00:21:06.119 --> 00:21:07.980
Had an affair with a studio exec.

00:21:07.980 --> 00:21:10.519
He uses her up, fires
her, leaves her destitute.

00:21:10.519 --> 00:21:14.519
Elise hangs herself from stage 9's rafters
right into a scene they're shooting.

00:21:14.519 --> 00:21:16.010
Just like our man Brad.

00:21:16.010 --> 00:21:17.949
So, what, she's got it
in for the studio brass?

00:21:17.949 --> 00:21:19.079
Possibly.

00:21:19.079 --> 00:21:22.530
I mean, it's a motive, and
Brad's death matches hers exactly.

00:21:22.530 --> 00:21:24.599
We're digging tonight, aren't we?

00:21:25.650 --> 00:21:27.199
That's a wrap, people!

00:21:27.199 --> 00:21:30.280
6:00 A.M.Call for crew tomorrow.

00:21:31.940 --> 00:21:33.500
Great work, everybody!

00:21:33.990 --> 00:21:36.750
Mcg, you're a genius.

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:39.190
You're kickin' ass and taking names.

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:40.440
Good night, Jay.

00:21:41.449 --> 00:21:42.510
Yeah.

00:21:45.139 --> 00:21:46.519
Which way?

00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:49.099
Over here.

00:21:55.369 --> 00:21:55.840
Hey.

00:21:55.880 --> 00:21:56.990
Yeah?

00:21:58.849 --> 00:22:01.719
Hey, this map is totally
worth the 5 bucks.

00:22:02.159 --> 00:22:05.119
Hey, we got to go check out Johnny
Ramone's grave when we're done here.

00:22:05.119 --> 00:22:06.829
You want to dig him up, too?

00:22:06.829 --> 00:22:09.190
Bite your tongue, heathen!

00:22:09.190 --> 00:22:12.179
You know, Dean, what I
don't get is, why now?

00:22:12.179 --> 00:22:15.909
I mean, after 75 years, Elise
Drummond suddenly goes homicidal.

00:22:15.909 --> 00:22:17.019
You know, why this movie?

00:22:17.019 --> 00:22:19.219
Well, maybe she's mad they're
making a scary ghost flick.

00:22:19.219 --> 00:22:20.610
Is it really that scary?

00:22:20.610 --> 00:22:21.659
Here we go.

00:22:25.690 --> 00:22:26.809
Yahtzee.

00:22:37.699 --> 00:22:38.250
I know.

00:22:38.250 --> 00:22:41.440
No, I friggin' hate mcg's dailies.

00:22:41.440 --> 00:22:42.800
I can't control the guy.

00:22:42.800 --> 00:22:46.079
I'm telling you -- Next
one I'm directing myself.

00:22:46.079 --> 00:22:48.019
What, you?

00:22:48.019 --> 00:22:49.119
No, bob.

00:22:49.119 --> 00:22:50.309
You I love.

00:22:50.309 --> 00:22:51.289
You're a genius.

00:22:51.289 --> 00:22:53.599
You're kicking ass and taking names.

00:22:53.599 --> 00:22:55.170
Yeah, okay.

00:22:55.170 --> 00:22:56.190
Yeah.

00:22:56.190 --> 00:22:57.240
Talk to you later, babe.

00:22:57.240 --> 00:22:58.519
Uh-Huh.

00:22:59.019 --> 00:23:00.389
What a dick.

00:23:01.760 --> 00:23:03.349
Oh, great.

00:23:06.190 --> 00:23:07.769
Hey, guys!

00:23:08.130 --> 00:23:09.730
Producer walking here!

00:23:09.730 --> 00:23:11.460
Hello!

00:24:08.980 --> 00:24:09.980
Hey!

00:24:12.159 --> 00:24:13.190
Hey, pal.

00:24:13.230 --> 00:24:15.300
Can you, uh, show me to the exit?

00:24:15.300 --> 00:24:17.510
I can't see a damn thing here.

00:24:21.740 --> 00:24:23.000
Hey!

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:24.280
Hey, putz.

00:24:24.280 --> 00:24:25.659
I'm talking to you.

00:24:25.719 --> 00:24:27.440
Somebody could get hurt here.

00:24:35.000 --> 00:24:36.420
What the hell?

00:24:47.190 --> 00:24:48.070
No!

00:24:52.409 --> 00:24:53.960
No!

00:25:22.340 --> 00:25:24.240
They never forgive.

00:25:25.440 --> 00:25:27.519
They never forget.

00:25:27.539 --> 00:25:28.760
Mitch?

00:25:29.269 --> 00:25:30.050
Ashley?

00:25:30.050 --> 00:25:33.960
This summer, they're coming
back again to settle the score...

00:25:33.960 --> 00:25:35.460
Again.

00:25:35.960 --> 00:25:37.400
You out here?

00:25:40.590 --> 00:25:42.019
Ashley and Todd
-- They're dead!

00:25:42.019 --> 00:25:43.170
Wendy, they're dead!

00:25:43.170 --> 00:25:45.750
These bastards aren't taking
us, not without a fight.

00:25:45.750 --> 00:25:47.260
I am getting out of here right now!

00:25:47.260 --> 00:25:48.449
Brody!

00:25:48.880 --> 00:25:51.190
From the makers of
"Cornfield Massacre"...

00:25:51.190 --> 00:25:54.409
"Monster truck, " "Charlie's angels"...

00:25:54.409 --> 00:25:55.869
"Charlie's Angels 2: Full throttle"...

00:25:55.869 --> 00:26:00.300
And "Hell hazers" comes a
new experience in terror.

00:26:01.240 --> 00:26:05.159
<i>We must have brought them
back ...back from hell. AGAIN</i>

00:26:08.670 --> 00:26:10.199
<i>This film not yet rated</i>

00:26:12.039 --> 00:26:14.079
Rolled in with a giant fan.

00:26:14.079 --> 00:26:18.099
Same thing happened to an electrician
back in '66 -- A guy named Billy Beard.

00:26:18.099 --> 00:26:19.429
What the hell, dude?

00:26:19.429 --> 00:26:20.070
I don't know.

00:26:20.070 --> 00:26:22.539
It doesn't seem like Elise this time.

00:26:22.539 --> 00:26:23.349
We already torched her.

00:26:23.349 --> 00:26:24.500
Are we dealing with another ghost?

00:26:24.500 --> 00:26:25.170
Maybe.

00:26:25.170 --> 00:26:27.159
Yeah, but these things
don't usually tag-Team.

00:26:31.369 --> 00:26:32.320
Everybody!

00:26:32.329 --> 00:26:33.909
Gather around, okay?

00:26:33.909 --> 00:26:35.500
I got an announcement to make.

00:26:35.650 --> 00:26:37.019
Hold that for me.

00:26:39.099 --> 00:26:40.130
Everyone!

00:26:40.599 --> 00:26:41.539
Huddle in!

00:26:44.679 --> 00:26:53.990
In light of Jay's accident last night and in cooperation with
the authorities, we're shutting down production for a few days.

00:26:54.510 --> 00:26:56.110
I know, I know.

00:26:56.110 --> 00:26:57.929
Look, I'm not going to lie to you.

00:26:57.929 --> 00:27:00.539
We've had a few setbacks this week.

00:27:00.539 --> 00:27:04.860
But we all know what Jay and
Brad wanted more than anything.

00:27:05.920 --> 00:27:11.490
And that was to see "Hell Hazers 2: The
Reckoning" on screens all across America.

00:27:11.769 --> 00:27:18.340
Now, we owe it to them to go on and to
pull together and make this damn movie, huh?

00:27:19.710 --> 00:27:22.710
But... but ... but ... but
...but not ... not today.

00:27:22.710 --> 00:27:24.440
Go home.

00:27:24.440 --> 00:27:26.199
Someone will call you.

00:27:30.349 --> 00:27:31.469
Wendy.

00:27:31.469 --> 00:27:33.849
What, are you afraid of ghosts?

00:27:33.849 --> 00:27:34.579
Come on.

00:27:34.579 --> 00:27:36.179
It'll be fun.

00:27:39.829 --> 00:27:41.050
Hey.

00:27:41.050 --> 00:27:42.269
Hey.

00:27:43.079 --> 00:27:45.650
So, you find out where
the electrician's buried?

00:27:45.650 --> 00:27:47.050
He wasn't.

00:27:47.050 --> 00:27:48.710
Billy beard was cremated.

00:27:48.710 --> 00:27:50.610
Great.

00:27:50.610 --> 00:27:52.050
Now what?

00:27:52.050 --> 00:27:53.389
No idea.

00:27:53.510 --> 00:27:55.769
Anymore ghost cameos in the dailies?

00:27:55.769 --> 00:27:58.199
Not in the first six hours.

00:27:59.380 --> 00:28:00.070
You know.

00:28:00.070 --> 00:28:04.219
Maybe the spirits are trying to shut
down the movie 'cause they think it sucks.

00:28:04.219 --> 00:28:05.750
'Cause, I mean, it kind of does.

00:28:05.750 --> 00:28:08.409
From, uh, "come on, it'll be fun"?

00:28:08.409 --> 00:28:09.199
Come on.

00:28:09.199 --> 00:28:10.559
It'll be fun.

00:28:24.699 --> 00:28:28.710
Listen to the invocation.

00:28:28.710 --> 00:28:33.420
Dean, that's the real deal a
necromantic summoning ritual.

00:28:36.539 --> 00:28:39.210
What the hell is that
doing in a hollywood movie?

00:28:39.210 --> 00:28:39.659
No, dear.

00:28:39.659 --> 00:28:40.940
We're down for a few days.

00:28:40.940 --> 00:28:45.599
It's cool, it gives me time to
pitch that time-Travel thing.

00:28:45.949 --> 00:28:46.800
Yeah.

00:28:46.840 --> 00:28:47.409
All right, well, look.

00:28:47.409 --> 00:28:48.429
Get back to me on this, all right?

00:28:48.429 --> 00:28:49.289
Seriously.

00:28:49.289 --> 00:28:51.030
No, I'm serious.

00:28:51.030 --> 00:28:52.130
Dude, are you serious?

00:28:52.130 --> 00:28:53.530
'Cause I'm serious.

00:28:53.530 --> 00:28:54.699
All right.

00:28:54.699 --> 00:28:55.820
Cool.

00:28:56.119 --> 00:28:57.039
Guys, we're all shut down.

00:28:57.039 --> 00:28:58.179
What are you still doing here?

00:28:58.179 --> 00:28:59.769
Yeah, uh...

00:28:59.769 --> 00:29:01.690
Really sorry, man.

00:29:01.690 --> 00:29:04.150
We -- We -- We
couldn't help ourselves.

00:29:04.150 --> 00:29:06.949
We just had to tell you
that we read the script.

00:29:06.949 --> 00:29:08.019
And?

00:29:08.940 --> 00:29:10.210
Yeah.

00:29:11.110 --> 00:29:12.510
It's, uh...

00:29:12.510 --> 00:29:13.409
It's awesome.

00:29:13.409 --> 00:29:14.610
Awesome.

00:29:14.610 --> 00:29:15.750
Really awesome.

00:29:15.750 --> 00:29:16.159
I know.

00:29:16.159 --> 00:29:17.309
It's pretty rockin', right?

00:29:17.309 --> 00:29:18.449
I'm glad you guys liked it.

00:29:18.449 --> 00:29:19.050
Yeah.

00:29:19.050 --> 00:29:21.849
I-I really liked all
the attention to detail.

00:29:21.849 --> 00:29:22.360
Dude, right on.

00:29:22.360 --> 00:29:22.880
That's my thing.

00:29:22.880 --> 00:29:25.170
I mean, you know, color
me guilty, but that is me.

00:29:25.170 --> 00:29:26.940
I'm a total detail buff.

00:29:26.940 --> 00:29:32.780
No, I mean, the way you worked in all those Enochian
summoning rituals and all the authentic language and...

00:29:32.780 --> 00:29:34.860
What, you mean that latin crap?

00:29:37.039 --> 00:29:37.590
No, man.

00:29:37.590 --> 00:29:38.780
That's Walter.

00:29:38.780 --> 00:29:40.900
Walter Dixon, the original writer.

00:29:40.900 --> 00:29:42.429
You like that garbage?

00:29:42.429 --> 00:29:43.990
Wait, Walter --
The P.A.Walter?

00:29:43.990 --> 00:29:45.030
No, he's not a P.A.

00:29:45.050 --> 00:29:47.969
He's got a clause in his contract
that allows him to come on set.

00:29:47.969 --> 00:29:49.519
But he wrote the invocations?

00:29:49.519 --> 00:29:51.230
He wrote a wackjob screenplay.

00:29:51.230 --> 00:29:51.900
There's no pace.

00:29:51.900 --> 00:29:53.000
There's no love interest.

00:29:53.000 --> 00:29:54.500
It's all wackadoo exposition.

00:29:54.500 --> 00:29:58.679
I had to cut, like, 90% of it to make
it readable, another 10% to make it good.

00:30:03.079 --> 00:30:04.960
Should have kept
Walter's original script.

00:30:04.960 --> 00:30:06.219
It's actually pretty good.

00:30:06.219 --> 00:30:07.829
Yeah.

00:30:09.210 --> 00:30:11.880
And it reads like a how-To
manual of conjuration,

00:30:11.880 --> 00:30:15.829
Like a textbook on how to summon ghosts
and get them to do whatever you want.

00:30:15.829 --> 00:30:17.050
Yeah, like kill people.

00:30:17.059 --> 00:30:18.380
Yep.

00:30:19.590 --> 00:30:22.619
So let's say somewhere down the line,
Walter learned some pretty black magic.

00:30:22.619 --> 00:30:26.230
Yeah, and let's say he's pissed at
these people for wrecking his movie.

00:30:26.490 --> 00:30:27.610
Motive and means.

00:30:28.119 --> 00:30:29.789
It's worth checking out.

00:30:39.730 --> 00:30:40.599
So?

00:30:42.190 --> 00:30:43.300
You wanted to meet?

00:30:45.980 --> 00:30:47.409
Hey, I'm a little busy here, buddy.

00:30:47.630 --> 00:30:48.679
I'm working on a script.

00:30:48.920 --> 00:30:49.179
Oh, yeah.

00:30:49.179 --> 00:30:50.929
You guys worked on it a lot.

00:30:50.929 --> 00:30:52.469
It needed work.

00:30:52.469 --> 00:30:54.240
Now, why couldn't we have
done this in my office?

00:30:54.240 --> 00:30:59.190
You know, the history, the lore in
my draft was completely accurate.

00:30:59.190 --> 00:31:06.010
We could have gotten it right for the first time ever
in this whorehouse of a town, but you tore it to shreds.

00:31:06.760 --> 00:31:10.130
You replaced it with
cleavage and fart jokes.

00:31:11.550 --> 00:31:12.789
It was real.

00:31:12.789 --> 00:31:15.219
Who gives a rat's ass about real?

00:31:15.219 --> 00:31:16.530
We're talking about ghosts here, Walter.

00:31:16.530 --> 00:31:17.460
There's no such thing.

00:31:17.460 --> 00:31:19.490
That's where you're wrong, martin.

00:31:31.420 --> 00:31:32.670
Okay, nutjob...

00:31:32.670 --> 00:31:33.969
End of meeting.

00:31:43.679 --> 00:31:45.059
C oh, my god, no!

00:31:45.059 --> 00:31:46.610
Please, no!

00:31:46.610 --> 00:31:48.360
You ruined it, martin!

00:31:48.360 --> 00:31:49.960
Everything I worked for!

00:31:49.960 --> 00:31:52.150
Oh, god!

00:31:52.480 --> 00:31:53.190
Walter!

00:31:53.190 --> 00:31:55.769
Now you're gonna find out
what being a ghost is like!

00:31:55.769 --> 00:31:57.269
Walter, please!

00:31:57.269 --> 00:31:59.289
Walter, help me!

00:31:59.740 --> 00:32:01.139
Help!

00:32:10.059 --> 00:32:12.000
You are one hell of a P.A.

00:32:12.000 --> 00:32:13.550
Yeah, I know.

00:32:15.880 --> 00:32:17.170
What are you doing?

00:32:17.309 --> 00:32:19.039
Could ask you the same thing, Walter.

00:32:19.039 --> 00:32:20.599
Raising these spirits from the dead?

00:32:21.940 --> 00:32:22.909
Making them murder for you?

00:32:22.909 --> 00:32:24.840
That's playing with fire, Walter.

00:32:24.840 --> 00:32:26.639
You don't understand.

00:32:27.809 --> 00:32:28.179
You know what?

00:32:28.179 --> 00:32:28.659
You're right.

00:32:28.659 --> 00:32:30.059
I don't understand.

00:32:31.909 --> 00:32:33.210
Wait, look.

00:32:33.210 --> 00:32:37.820
You put your heart and soul into
something, years of hard work ... years.

00:32:37.820 --> 00:32:41.440
And then they take it,
and they crap all over it!

00:32:42.440 --> 00:32:45.660
And then -- And then they want
you to smile and say thank you.

00:32:45.660 --> 00:32:46.280
Walter, listen.

00:32:46.280 --> 00:32:47.110
It's just a movie.

00:32:47.110 --> 00:32:48.280
That's it.

00:32:51.900 --> 00:32:52.769
Look.

00:32:54.800 --> 00:32:56.180
I got nothing against you, man.

00:32:56.180 --> 00:32:57.110
You're not part of this.

00:32:57.110 --> 00:32:59.400
Just please --
Please, just leave.

00:33:00.079 --> 00:33:01.430
But martin's got to stay.

00:33:01.630 --> 00:33:03.010
Sorry, can't do that.

00:33:03.340 --> 00:33:04.610
It's not that we like him or anything.

00:33:04.610 --> 00:33:06.940
It's a matter of principle.

00:33:06.940 --> 00:33:08.630
Then I'm sorry, too.

00:33:09.800 --> 00:33:10.630
Walter.

00:33:10.630 --> 00:33:12.780
Walter,
pl-- Don't.

00:33:33.120 --> 00:33:34.519
Sam!

00:33:44.309 --> 00:33:44.860
Come on.

00:33:44.860 --> 00:33:46.170
Come on.

00:33:56.300 --> 00:33:58.190
Come out to the coast.

00:34:12.070 --> 00:34:15.610
We'll get together, have a few laughs.

00:34:20.990 --> 00:34:22.110
Oh, man!

00:34:23.700 --> 00:34:24.630
I can't frickin' believe this.

00:34:24.630 --> 00:34:25.640
Ghosts are real.

00:34:25.640 --> 00:34:26.980
What makes you say that?

00:34:37.510 --> 00:34:38.430
But I don't understand.

00:34:38.620 --> 00:34:40.620
How is Walter controlling them?

00:34:40.760 --> 00:34:42.420
Probably that talisman.

00:34:49.690 --> 00:34:50.539
What are you doing?

00:34:50.539 --> 00:34:53.289
If film cameras pick
these suckers up, then...

00:34:53.289 --> 00:34:55.090
Maybe, uh...

00:35:00.510 --> 00:35:01.820
Dean, right there!

00:35:08.269 --> 00:35:08.760
Hey!

00:35:08.760 --> 00:35:10.030
Right there!

00:35:15.470 --> 00:35:15.880
Here.

00:35:15.880 --> 00:35:16.510
Get the idea?

00:35:16.510 --> 00:35:16.980
Yeah.

00:35:16.980 --> 00:35:17.829
All right, you hold them off.

00:35:17.829 --> 00:35:19.320
I'm going after Walter.

00:35:24.300 --> 00:35:26.090
I cannot believe there's an afterlife.

00:35:26.090 --> 00:35:27.829
There's an afterlife, all right.

00:35:27.829 --> 00:35:29.860
But mostly it's a pain in the ass.

00:35:31.590 --> 00:35:32.579
There!

00:35:36.940 --> 00:35:39.900
It's over, Walter.

00:35:43.599 --> 00:35:44.590
TherE.

00:35:44.730 --> 00:35:46.420
Okay, now no one can have it.

00:35:48.950 --> 00:35:50.720
I wouldn't have done that if I were you.

00:35:50.720 --> 00:35:51.970
Yeah?

00:35:51.970 --> 00:35:53.039
Why not?

00:35:53.140 --> 00:35:54.620
'Cause you just freed them.

00:35:55.480 --> 00:35:57.210
We can't stop them now.

00:35:57.650 --> 00:35:59.370
Walter, you brought them back...

00:36:00.099 --> 00:36:01.530
Forced them to murder.

00:36:01.910 --> 00:36:03.870
They're not going to
be very happy with you.

00:36:03.870 --> 00:36:05.200
Yeah?

00:36:05.519 --> 00:36:06.590
So, why not?

00:36:28.280 --> 00:36:31.620
Oh, god.

00:36:33.640 --> 00:36:34.730
There!

00:36:36.390 --> 00:36:37.400
But I don't understand.

00:36:37.680 --> 00:36:39.740
How come the spirits
appear in the camera phone?

00:36:39.740 --> 00:36:42.710
The video must pick up their
frequencies in a way that our eyes can't.

00:36:45.440 --> 00:36:46.840
Oh, God.

00:36:46.960 --> 00:36:48.010
Right there!

00:36:50.570 --> 00:36:51.300
Cut!

00:36:51.300 --> 00:36:52.870
Oh, print that one.

00:36:52.870 --> 00:36:54.099
That's in the movie.

00:36:54.099 --> 00:36:54.740
Oh!

00:36:54.740 --> 00:36:56.329
Loved it, kids,  loved it!

00:37:00.120 --> 00:37:03.030
You find out there's an afterlife,
and this is what you do with it?

00:37:04.090 --> 00:37:05.980
<i>I needed a little jazz on the page.</i>

00:37:25.849 --> 00:37:27.519
You're one hell of a P.A.

00:37:29.190 --> 00:37:30.240
Thank you.

00:37:33.300 --> 00:37:34.289
Hi.

00:37:58.630 --> 00:38:00.000
<i>God, I love this town.</i>



